
Report = 1776        Program = BPP.EXE       MKT1.1     04/08/91

GROUP names used in the simulation sections are not expanded into individual
signal names.

work-a-around: none
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1866,1872   Program = BPP.EXE       MKT1.1     04/23/91

Extended memory version aborts with error GP AT 002F 4844 EC 0000.
Extended memory version aborts with error GP AT 00AF 4984 EC 4F7C.

work-a-around:
        Switch off the automatic pairing option (ie set = 'N') found in the
        menu under the Setup/Logic Synthesis Options.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1877        Program = BPP.EXE       MKT1.1     05/06/91

Tristate equation generated with slash (ie. '/') when included inside an
IF-THEN-ELSE or CASE expression.

work-a-around:
        Functional equations (eg. .TRST,.CLKF,.SETF,.RSTF) should not be
        specified inside IF-THEN-ELSE or CASE logical constructs.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1916        Program = BPP.EXE       MKT1.1     05/23/91

Large CASE constructs,(ie. typically with >20 blocks), cause both undetected
and detected out-of-memory problems in this program.

work-a-round:
        Break up the large CASE constructs into small multiple constructs by
        doing:     CASE (conditions) BEGIN
                             ...
                   END
                   OTHERWISE  BEGIN
                              CASE (conditions) BEGIN
                                     ...
                              END
                   END
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1769        Program = MAINMENU.EXE       MKT1.1     04/05/91

If CTL-S is hit while the menu is compiling a design the current step finishes
and the stops the PC system.

work-a-round:
        Press CNTL-C to continue the processing, <ESC> halts the process step.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 653         Program = MINIMIZE.EXE       ALPHA      07/27/90

Large single equation with > 26 unique signals in the expression will cause
the program to hang the PC system.

Work-a-round: none.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1346        Program = MINIMIZE.EXE       ALPHA      10/10/90

Extremely large equations may cause error message:
 'SYSTEM ERROR 27 ALLOCATING MEMORY BLOCK GREATER THAN 64K.

Work-a-round: none.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1396        Program = MINIMIZE.EXE       MKT1.0     10/30/90

Program produces a runtime error when trying to gate split an equation with
greater than 99 product terms.

Work-a-round: none.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1943        Program = PALXPT.EXE         MKT1.1     06/04/91

Program programs incorrectly the J-K & R-S equations when the signal is
defined with a slash in the pin list declaration for the PALCE610 device. Bad
JEDEC is produced.

Work-a-round:
        Define all J-K & R-S output with no slash in the pin list declaration.
        Use polarity settings only on the RHS of the equation definition.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1742        Program = PARSE.EXE          MKT1.1     02/21/91

An .T registered equation if defined with the latch operator (*=) is not
syntactically trapped as an error. Software continues assuming T registered
equation.

Work-a-round: none.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1833        Program = PARSE.EXE          MKT1.1     04/19/91

A syntax error, (ie missing '+' operator in boolean equation) was trapped
incorrectly as an error associated with the STATE section.

Work-a-round: none.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1835        Program = PARSE.EXE          MKT1.1     04/19/91


A syntax error, (ie incorrect spelling of keyword 'SIMULATION') was trapped
incorrectly as an error associated with the SETF statement.

Work-a-round: none.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1890        Program = PARSE.EXE          MKT1.1     05/10/91

A syntax error in the power-up definition of a state machine design is not
trapped by the program. This leads to EXPAND.EXE aborting with an internal
corruption error.

Work-a-round:
        Avoid syntax error definition:
                STARTUP = vcc -> S0

        should be:
                STARTUP = POWERUP -> S0
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Report = 1899        Program = PARSE.EXE          MKT1.1     05/16/91

A syntax error, (ie. define signal set as A[1-5] instead of A[1..5]) is not
trapped by the software. This leads to BPP.EXE aborting with an internal
corruption error.

